  "result": "Quiz 0002 is ready, with its key. It has six items on O4:\n\n- **Files:** `quizzes/0002.json` and `keys/0002.json`.\n- **Types:** three multiple-choice items, one numeric item and two short-answer items.\n- **Content:** the items cover who owns the control flow, spotting a fixed workflow in your makerspace assistant, choosing which part of the assistant should be a workflow, comparing cost per request, and when an agent is worth it.\n- **Source:** the definitions come from Anthropic's \"Building effective agents\".\n- **Ahead of the lessons:** no lesson covers O4 yet, so this quiz checks the objective itself. I can write a lesson on it if you want one.\n- **New misconception ids:** I used M7 for treating a feature (several model calls, tools or memory) as what makes an agent. I used M8 for assuming harder tasks or agents are always better. Neither id existed before, and the key marks the options that encode them.\n\nI didn't edit `NOTES.md`, because the quiz hasn't been taken yet.\n\nDo you want to take the quiz now in the chat?",
